# scripts/check-legacy-naming.allowlist — exceptions for the rename
# verification script (0.31.0 lode/cairn/echo/sigil/stones; 0.50.0
# swarmcast/swarmgit/swarmresolve/swarmreg → filecast/gitback/hostdox/curator).
#
# Format:
#   <path>:<line>:<token>   exact-line allowlist
#   <path>:*:<token>        whole-file allowlist (ignore every match in this file)
#
# Paths are matched exactly against `git ls-files` output, so they must
# carry the full repo-relative path. The 2026-05-13 docs restructure
# moved internal docs under docs/internal.docs/ — entries below reflect
# that. If a doc moves again, its entry here must move with it or the
# checker turns red on otherwise-allowlisted files.
#
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are comments.
# For whole-file entries the third field is cosmetic (the script keys
# on the path only); for exact-line entries it must be the matched
# token regex as printed by the script (e.g. `\bcairn\b`).
#
# Add a line here only when the legacy term is genuinely unavoidable —
# typically: historical commit messages preserved in completed.md, the
# user's literal disk-layout path, or test fixtures that deliberately
# probe the legacy terminology.

# completed.md is the historical record — every entry there is from
# before its surrounding rename and stays as-it-was for accuracy.
# Memory files live outside the repo working tree (in
# ~/.claude/projects/...) so `git ls-files` doesn't return them; this
# entry is a safety net in case future tooling brings them in.
.claude/projects/-home-dan-repos-vigo/memory/completed.md:*:cairn

# The rename plan documents describe their renames — every legacy term
# appears as part of the mapping description. Allowlisted wholesale.
docs/internal.docs/plan-substrate-rename.md:*:cairn
docs/internal.docs/plan-rename-2026-05.md:*:swarmgit

# The France GTM plan lists "Cairn" as a product name in its glossary
# section; that prose was authored before the rename. Future pass.
docs/internal.docs/plan-france-linux-migration-gtm.md:*:cairn

# multi-axis-audit.md references the memory directory absolute path
# (Dan's literal workstation path).
docs/internal.docs/multi-axis-audit.md:*:cairn

# Historical probe scripts under docs/internal.docs/ targeting the old
# sigil subsystem. They no longer run — vigo sigil verbs were folded
# into `vigo swarm lockbox`. Kept as historical context until Dan
# deletes.
docs/internal.docs/sigil-peers-probe.sh:*:sigil
docs/internal.docs/sigil-tombstone-probe.sh:*:sigil

# Substrate audit + phase-rollout docs were authored under the legacy
# vocabulary. They describe the substrate before this rename and stay
# as-was for historical accuracy.
docs/internal.docs/substrate-audit.md:*:cairn
docs/internal.docs/substrate-livetest-all.sh:*:cairn
docs/internal.docs/substrate-livetests.md:*:cairn
docs/internal.docs/substrate-perms-repair.sh:*:cairn
docs/internal.docs/substrate-phase-b-deploy.sh:*:cairn
docs/internal.docs/substrate-phase-b-livetest.md:*:cairn
docs/internal.docs/substrate-phase-b-livetest.sh:*:cairn
docs/internal.docs/substrate-phase-b.md:*:cairn
docs/internal.docs/substrate-phase-c-livetest.sh:*:cairn
docs/internal.docs/substrate-phase-d-livetest.sh:*:cairn
docs/internal.docs/substrate-unified-plan.md:*:cairn

# scripts/migrate-0.30.sh handles upgrades from 0.29.x to 0.30.x and
# references the older state-on-disk paths.
scripts/migrate-0.30.sh:*:cairn

# The verification script itself contains the legacy tokens as the
# patterns it greps for.
scripts/check-legacy-naming.sh:*:cairn

# The factory-reset substrate test deliberately names the retired
# per-user state dirs (.vigo-swarmgit, .vigo-cairn, .vigorepo, …) in its
# USER_DIRS wipe list and the comments describing it, so leftover state
# from pre-0.50.0 enrollments gets scrubbed before the e2e runs from a
# clean slate. Rewriting these would make the wipe stop cleaning those
# dirs. Whole-file because the wipe list + its comments are edited often.
test/swarm-substrate.sh:*:swarmgit

# Pre-existing references to the historical "cairn"-era reset incident —
# the tshoot archive file is named log-archive-cairn-resolved-20260424-…
# (its name can't change), and the prose pointing at it cites it by that
# name. Not introduced by the 0.50.0 rename; allowlisted by line so the
# checker stays green.
server/grpc/agentstream.go:992:\bcairn\b
server/swarm/manifest.go:54:\bcairn\b
server/swarm/manifest.go:292:\bcairn\b

# The 2026-06-14 per-subsystem code-review doc quotes the retired "swarmgit"
# path in its description of finding U5 (a stale comment in tessera payload.go).
# The code occurrence was fixed 2026-06-15; the review doc keeps the original
# finding text as a historical record, so allowlist that one line.
docs/internal.docs/code-review-by-subsystem-2026-06-14.md:405:\bswarmgit\b

# The config loader hard-errors on the retired 0.66.0 federation keys
# (tungol → spanner, steorra → bolt). These lines ARE the migration
# guard + its doc comment — they must name the retired keys to detect
# and reject them. The reversion plan doc records the experiment.
docs/internal.docs/plans/vigo-plan-spanner-redesign-2026-05-16.md:33:\btungol
server/config/server.go:204:\btungol
server/config/server.go:205:\bsteorra
server/config/server.go:230:\btungol
server/config/server.go:235:\bTungol
server/config/server.go:238:\btungol
